  "conditions": "Conditional final flight after Guillermo enters the room behind the mirror, takes the poisoned book, is revealed to be wearing the gloves, and Jorge's state-0x0f delay reaches 0x28. Jorge is scripted into the mirror room at Night VI and remains at that fixed position throughout the preceding stationary states; the activation/reposition is not a walked segment. The same 127-point source trace was separately verified with combined mask 0x1f for Night VI, Compline VI, and Night VII, and with 0x2f for Prima-Vespers VI and Prima VII. It may therefore begin in any listed phase once the player-dependent encounter completes, rather than canonically at Night VII. On arrival Jorge waits for Guillermo to reach screen 0x67 below height 0x1e; only then does the code mark failure and the investigation complete (the source describes this as where Jorge dies). That terminal condition is not an additional walked segment. Day-VII Tercia is excluded because the Abbot's deadline branch ends the investigation. Static floor geometry, no actor or door-leaf collisions.",
